ith low, intermediate and high risk. (<bold>B</bold>) AJCC stage IV classification: M1a, normal lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) and metastases confined to the skin and lymph nodes, M1b including lung metastases and normal LDH and M1c including other visceral organs or elevated serum LDH.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="gif" xlink:href="93-6602702f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Univariate Cox's analyses of risk factors and survival in metastatic melanoma</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/><col align="char" char="."/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="3" align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Univariate Cox's analyses</bold></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Risk factors</bold></th><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Categories compared</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Number of patients</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>Hazard ratio</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; CI</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" char="." charoff="50"><bold><italic>P</italic>-value</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Gender</td><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Female <italic>vs</italic> male</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">181 <italic>vs</italic> 140</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">1.0</td><td align="char" valign="top" char="." charoff="50">0.8&#x